s, railings for commercial market -> /", "Ships products anywhere in US, erects within 200 miles of Louisville KY -> /", "Works with manufacturing facilities for structural and miscellaneous steel fabrication and erection -> /", "Locally owned and operated -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Today, the company encompasses a 36,000 square foot manufacturing facility and provides design, engineering, fabrication, and full erection for both residential and commercial projects.", "founded_year": "2005", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='sonne-steel' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Sonoco Plastics, based in Greer, South Carolina, traces its roots to 1946 when it was established as the Industrial & Specialty Plastics division of Sonoco Products Company (NYSE: SON).

The company specializes in plastic injection molding, extrusion, and assembly, supported by in-house design, engineering, and quality teams. Its capabilities include high-speed automation molding, insert and overmolding, two-shot robotic production, in-mold labeling, and food-grade molding. Sonoco also provides tool design, prototyping, mold making, and multi-process integration for efficient assembly of components such as living hinges, multi-piece assemblies, and fuse collars.

Sonoco serves automotive manufacturers requiring ISO/IATF 16949:2016-compliant parts, medical device makers needing ISO Class 7 and 8 cleanroom components, and filtration markets with engineered cores and cages. It also supplies FSSC 22000-certified consumer and pharmaceutical packaging, foodservice smallware for quick-service restaurants (including patented Accu-Salt and Accu-Taste dispensers), and industrial products such as spools, reels, cores, endwalls, and textile carriers for wire and cable.

The division emphasizes innovation and speed, promoting the fastest turnaround times in the industry and a model that moves projects from concept to production quickly through integrated design, engineering, and quality support.', certifications=ARRAY['IATF 16949:2016','FSSC 22000','ISO Class 7','ISO Class 8']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Plastic injection molding", "Plastic extrusion", "Assembly", "In-house design and engineering", "Quality support", "High-speed automation molding", "Insert molding", "Overmolding", "Two-shot automated robotic production", "In-mold labeling", "Food-grade molding", "Tool design", "Mold making", "Prototyping", "Living hinge design", "Multi-piece component assembly", "Automated molding with insert capabilities", "Multi-process integration"], "industries": ["Automotive", "Medical", "Filtration", "Consumer packaging", "Pharmaceutical packaging", "Foodservice", "Industrial", "Consumer packaged goods"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Fastest turnaround times in the industry", "In-house design, engineering, and quality support", "Two-shot automated robotic production", "FSSC 22000-certified consumer and pharmaceutical packaging", "ISO Class 7 and 8 cleanroom medical components"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1946 -> /", "Headquartered in Greer, South Carolina -> db", "Division of Sonoco Products Company (NYSE: SON) -> /", "Global manufacturer of custom and proprietary plastic solutions -> /", "Capabilities: injection molding, extrusion, assembly, in-house design, engineering, quality support -> /", "High-speed automation molding, insert molding, overmolding, two-shot automated robotic production -> /", "In-mold labeling, food-grade molding, tool design, prototyping, mold making -> /", "Industries: automotive (ISO/IATF 16949:2016), medical (ISO Class 7/8 cleanroom), filtration, consumer/pharmaceutical packaging (FSSC 22000), foodservice, industrial (spools, reels, cores, endwalls, textile carriers) -> /", "Certifications: IATF 16949:2016, FSSC 22000, ISO Class 7, ISO Class 8 -> /, db", "Emphasis on fastest turnaround times and integrated concept-to-production -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Sonoco Industrial & Specialty Plastics\u2014a division of Sonoco Products Company (NYSE: SON)\u2014is a global manufacturer of custom and proprietary plastic solutions.", "founded_year": "1946", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='sonoco-plastics' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Sota Metal Fabrication LLC operates from Burnsville, Minnesota. The business traces its roots to 2010, when Steve acquired Air Pro, LLC after the death of its founder Michael McFarland and relaunched it as Chimney Doctors.

The company manufactures a full range of custom chimney components including full-coverage caps, shrouds, pots, shoulder guards, gable and barrel roof caps, chase covers, and crickets. All products are fabricated to custom measurements in the company''s local facility using a no-weld construction method on caps. The shop also provides design and engineering support for unique chimney challenges.

The firm also sells directly to homeowners seeking code-compliant protection for masonry and factory-built chimneys.

Steve''s original vision was to bring transparency and education to chimney service. That mission carries into the product line: every ChimGuard item carries a lifetime replacement warranty, and the full-coverage cap design is intended to eliminate return trips by fitting correctly the first time.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom chimney cap fabrication", "Chimney shroud manufacturing", "Chimney pot fabrication", "Shoulder guard fabrication", "Gable roof chimney cap fabrication", "Barrel roof chimney cap fabrication", "Chase cover fabrication", "Cricket fabrication", "Custom product design and engineering", "Metal fabrication for chimney systems"], "industries": ["Chimney and fireplace industry", "Hearth services", "Residential construction", "Roofing", "Real estate inspection"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Lifetime replacement warranty on all ChimGuard products", "Custom-made to exact field measurements", "No-weld construction on chimney caps", "Full-coverage cap design eliminates return trips", "Products manufactured in local Burnsville facility"], "facts_used": ["Company name Sota Metal Fabrication LLC -> db", "Headquarters Burnsville, Minnesota -> db", "Founded 2010 as Chimney Doctors after Steve purchased Air Pro -> db", "Owner Steve -> db", "Manufactures custom chimney caps, shrouds, pots, shoulder guards, chase covers, crickets -> db, /", "Products made in local facility -> db, /", "No-weld construction on caps -> /", "Lifetime replacement warranty -> db, /", "Custom measurements -> db", "Serves chimney and fireplace industry, contractors, homeowners, real estate -> db", "Full-coverage cap design eliminates return trips -> /", "Precision-built components for first-time fit -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We can design and manufacture a product to meet your need", "founded_year": "2010", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='sota-metal-fabrication-llc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Sound Manufacturing, Inc. was founded in 1984 in Old Saybrook, Connecticut, by Brian Cote and Kenneth Oliver. Now a three‑generation family business, the company has been led since 2006 by President and CEO Kelli‑Marie Vallieres, PhD (through 2020) and, since 2020, by President/COO John Vallieres. From its start as a local sheet metal fabrication partner, it has grown into a contract manufacturer serving clients across New England and beyond.

The shop provides precision sheet metal fabrication including laser cutting (Trumpf CO₂ and fiber lasers up to 5 kW), CNC punching (Trumpf TruMatic 3000 and TruPunch 5000), forming and bending on Trumpf press brakes up to 10 ft, TIG/MIG/spot welding, deburring and finishing (Lissmac, Timesaver, tumbling), PEM and rivet hardware installation, CNC milling and turning (DN Solutions, Haas), inspection, and assembly/packing. With 40‑plus team members, the facility runs 24/7, holds ±0.005 in dimensional tolerance, processes material up to 1 in thick, and handles short‑run to full‑production volumes, having produced over 10 million parts to date.

Customers span telecommunications (server racks, patch panels, enclosures), green energy (bus bars, breaker panels, EV‑charging components, power‑storage housings), defense, automation (robotic bases, control boxes, sensor brackets), packaging (tape‑machine and packaging‑machine components), outdoor power equipment (OEM frames, impellers, leaf boxes for Monster Power Equipment), industrial machinery (welded frames, guarding), data‑center infrastructure, and electrical distribution. The client base ranges from startups to Tier 1 manufacturers; long‑term partners include Intertape Polymer Group and robotics firm Cavalla.

The company emphasizes a quality‑as‑culture approach backed by ISO 9001:2015 certification and a reported 99 %‑plus on‑time delivery rate. It cites decades of craftsmanship, continuous investment in advanced Trumpf and CNC equipment, and a commitment to environmental responsibility—including a 30 % CO₂ reduction target for Scope 1 & 2 by 2030—as key differentiators.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Laser Cutting (CO2 and fiber, up to 5 kW)", "CNC Punching (Trumpf TruMatic 3000, TruPunch 5000)", "Forming & Bending (Trumpf press brakes up to 10 ft)", "Welding (TIG, MIG, Spot)", "Finishing & Deburring (Lissmac, Timesaver, tumbling)", "Hardware Installation (PEM, Rivet)", "CNC Machining (Milling, Turning - DN Solutions, Haas)", "Quality Inspection (ISO 9001:2015)", "Assembly & Packing"], "industries": ["Telecommunication", "Green Energy", "Defense", "Automation", "Packaging", "Outdoor Power Equipment", "Industrial Machinery", "Data Center", "Electrical Distribution"], "materials": ["Steel", "Stainless Steel", "Aluminum", "Copper"], "equipment": ["Trumpf CO2 and fiber lasers (3-5 kW)", "Trumpf TruMatic 3000 combo machine", "Trumpf TruPunch 5000", "Trumpf press brakes (up to 10 ft)", "Lissmac deburring machine", "Two-stage tumbling process", "Timesaver finishing machine", "DN Solutions CNC machines", "Haas CNC machines"], "volume": "Short run to production volumes", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "\u00b10.005 in", "built_on": ["ISO 9001:2015 certified with rigorous quality control processes", "Over 99% on-time delivery rate", "24/7 production capabilities", "\u00b10.005\" dimensional tolerance", "Three-generation family ownership with 40+ years experience"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1984 in Old Saybrook, Connecticut -> /about", "Three-generation family business -> /about", "Founders Brian Cote and Kenneth Oliver -> /about", "Leadership: Kelli-Marie Vallieres, PhD (President/CEO 2006-2020), John Vallieres (President/COO since 2020) -> /about", "ISO 9001:2015 certified -> /about, /services", "40+ years experience, 250+ satisfied clients, 10M+ parts manufactured, 40+ team members -> /about", "Services: laser cutting, CNC punching, forming/bending, welding, finishing/deburring, hardware installation, CNC machining, quality inspection, assembly/packing -> /services", "Equipment: Trumpf lasers, Trumpf TruMatic 3000, TruPunch 5000, Trumpf press brakes, Lissmac deburring, Timesaver finishing, DN Solutions, Haas -> /services", "Materials: Steel, Stainless Steel, Aluminum, Copper -> /services", "Tolerance: \u00b10.005\" -> /services", "24/7 production capabilities -> /services", "Short run to production volumes -> /services", "Industries: telecommunication, green energy, defense, automation, packaging, outdoor power equipment, industrial machines, data center, electrical distribution -> /, /about", "Customer examples: Intertape Polymer Group, Cavalla -> /", "CO2 emission reduction target 30% by 2030 -> /about", "Over 99% on-time delivery rate -> /"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Since our founding in 1984 in Old Saybrook, Connecticut, Sound Manufacturing, Inc. has grown into a respected leader in contract manufacturing", "founded_year": "1984", "employee_count": "40+", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='sound-manufacturing-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='South Coast Controls, Inc. operates from a 38,000-square-foot facility in Anaheim, California. The company was founded in 1984 and remains family-owned, focusing on precision automation and control solutions for mission-critical applications.

The shop manufactures UL 508A, UL 698A, and UL 1203 listed control panels, including hazardous-location and purge systems, and provides PLC/HMI programming (Allen-Bradley, Siemens, Schneider Electric, Modicon), SCADA development (Ignition, Wonderware, FactoryTalk View SE, iFIX), and enclosure modification via a Steinhauer CNC ModCenter. A team of 25-plus technicians handles wire harness fabrication, panel assembly, UL labeling, and 100% functional testing, with engineering support for heat calculations, NEMA/IP ratings, short-circuit analysis, and arc flash studies. The facility has delivered over 168,000 projects since inception.

Primary markets include utilities, water treatment, and general industrial automation.

The company emphasizes a four-stage workflow—design engineering, software development, fabrication, and delivery—with UL compliance and full testing built in. Standard manufacturing lead times run six to twelve weeks, while engineering quotes are returned within 24 hours. Global shipping is offered alongside local delivery in Southern California using a company fleet.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','UL 508A','UL 698A','UL 1203','CSA Certified']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["UL 508A/698A/1203 control panel manufacturing", "PLC/HMI programming (Allen-Bradley, Siemens, Schneider Electric, Modicon)", "SCADA development (Ignition, Wonderware, FactoryTalk View SE, iFIX)", "Hazardous location panel design (Class I Div 1/2, Class II Div 1/2)", "Enclosure CNC modification (Steinhauer ModCenter)", "Wire harness fabrication", "Panel assembly and UL labeling", "100% functional testing", "Engineering analysis (heat calculations, NEMA/IP ratings, short-circuit, arc flash)", "Legacy system migration", "Robot integration", "Installation and commissioning", "Custom purge panel manufacturing", "Lighting control panel manufacturing"], "industries": ["Utilities", "Water treatment", "Industrial automation"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Steinhauer CNC modification center (ModCenter)"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "6-12 weeks for manufacturing; 24-hour quote turnaround", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["UL 508A/698A/1203 listed shop with ISO 9001:2015 certification", "38,000 sq ft facility with Steinhauer CNC modification center", "24-hour engineering quote turnaround", "6-12 week standard lead times with global shipping", "Family-owned since 1984 with 25+ technicians"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1984 -> db", "Headquarters Anaheim, CA -> db", "Family-owned since 1984 -> /", "38,000 sq ft facility -> /", "25+ technicians -> /", "168,000+ projects delivered -> /", "ISO 9001:2015 certified -> db, /", "UL 508A, 698A, 1203 certified -> db, /", "Services: control panel manufacturing, PLC/HMI programming, SCADA, hazardous location, enclosure modification -> /", "Steinhauer CNC modification center -> /", "Lead times 6-12 weeks -> /", "Quote turnaround 24 hours -> /", "Global shipping, local delivery -> /", "Installation and commissioning available -> /", "Industries: utilities, water treatment, industrial automation -> /", "Four-stage workflow -> /", "CSA Certified -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "UL 508A, UL 698A, UL 1203 certified control panel manufacturing. 38,000 sq ft facility. 25+ technicians. Steinhauer CNC modification center for enclosure work. ISO 9001:2015 certified. 100% functional testing, UL labeling, quality control.", "founded_year": "1984", "employee_count": "25+", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='south-coast-controls-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='South Sound Solar, Inc. has operated from Olympia, Washington since its founding in 2007. The company serves the South Sound region as a full-service solar and energy storage installer.

The firm functions as an electrical and general contractor, providing system design, installation, and ongoing service for residential and commercial photovoltaic arrays, battery backup systems, and electric vehicle charging stations. Its scope includes site assessment using professional shade analysis tools, custom proposal development, array repair, panel cleaning, and troubleshooting for monitoring systems, including equipment originally installed by other providers.

Customers range from homeowners seeking to reduce electricity costs to commercial property owners pursuing sustainability goals. The company regularly coordinates with Puget Sound Energy''s solar calculator program and serves clients throughout Thurston County and the broader Pacific Northwest.

South Sound Solar emphasizes a single-point-of-responsibility model, handling design, installation, and long-term maintenance in-house. It offers free site surveys and aims to present options without sales pressure, positioning itself as a local resource for both new projects and orphaned systems.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Solar photovoltaic system design", "Solar photovoltaic system installation", "Battery backup system installation", "Electric vehicle charger installation", "Solar array repair and maintenance", "Solar panel cleaning", "Shade analysis and site assessment", "Custom solar proposal development", "System monitoring troubleshooting", "Electrical contracting", "General contracting"], "industries": ["Residential solar", "Commercial solar", "Battery energy storage", "Electric vehicle charging infrastructure", "Renewable energy"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["System design, installation, and long-term service under one roof", "Service and repair for systems installed by other companies", "Free site surveys with professional shade analysis", "Licensed electrical and general contractor", "Coordination with Puget Sound Energy solar programs"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2007 in Olympia, Washington -> db and /", "Full-service solar and storage installer -> /", "Electrical and general contractor -> /services", "Services: system design, installation, battery backup, EV chargers, repair, cleaning -> / and /services", "Service for systems installed by other companies -> /", "Free site surveys offered -> / and /services", "Professional shade analysis tools used -> /services", "Works with Puget Sound Energy solar calculator -> /about-us", "Serves residential and commercial customers -> / and /services", "20 years serving South Sound neighbors -> /"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "South Sound Solar is a full service Storage & solar installer located in Olympia, Washington.", "founded_year": "2007", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='south-sound-solar-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='SouthLoft Crafted Concepts operates from Euless, Texas. The company traces its roots to 2014, when founder Colby Murphy began building furniture as a hobby in his father’s garage. That garage start has since grown into a full-scale production shop serving commercial and residential clients nationwide.

The shop produces custom furniture for both commercial and residential spaces. Its capabilities span design consultation, material sourcing, fabrication, finishing, and after-sale support. SouthLoft offers a line of ready-made pieces that can be customized, as well as fully bespoke builds. The operation now runs as a large-scale facility, though specific square footage and headcount are not disclosed.

The client base centers on the hospitality sector, with restaurant projects for chains such as Gloria’s Latin Cuisine, 60 Vines, Musume, and Fogo de Chão. The company also works with owners, designers, and architects on commercial interiors and private residences, exemplified by residential packages like The Bellomy Package.

SouthLoft emphasizes a quality-first mindset, describing its mission as bringing back products made with heart and soul. The founder stresses that every step — from initial consultation through material selection and final delivery — matters. The company holds its material vendors to high standards, aiming to distinguish its output from mass-produced alternatives.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom furniture manufacturing", "Commercial furniture production", "Residential furniture production", "Design and engineering", "Material sourcing and selection", "Finishing services", "Project management", "Consultation and project planning", "Ready-made product customization"], "industries": ["Hospitality", "Restaurant", "Commercial", "Residential"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Quality-first mindset across all products", "End-to-end process: consultation, material selection, design, build, after-sale support", "High standards for vendor-sourced materials", "Collaboration with owners, designers, and architects", "From garage hobby to national commercial and residential client base"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2014 as a hobby in founder''s garage -> /about", "Founder: Colby Murphy -> /about", "Headquarters: Euless, Texas -> db", "Custom furniture manufacturer for commercial and residential projects -> /", "Commercial projects include Gloria''s Latin Cuisine, 60 Vines, Musume, Fogo de Ch\u00e3o -> /", "Residential projects include The Bellomy Package -> /", "Offers ready-made products and fully custom pieces -> /", "Quality-first mindset, attention to detail -> /about", "End-to-end process: consultation, material selection, design, build, after-sale support -> /about", "Team includes Nolen Mares (Director of Operations), Brandon Vaughn (Project Director) -> /about", "Works with owners, designers, and architects -> /", "Clients across United States -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We are a custom furniture manufacturer for commercial and residential projects.", "founded_year": "2014", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='southloft-crafted-concepts' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Southeastern Butcher Supplies, Inc. operates from Pelham, Alabama, where it serves as a dealer for meat processing machinery and a supplier of related parts and consumables. The company''s founding year and ownership structure are not publicly disclosed.

The business stocks equipment from multiple manufacturers, offers replacement parts for various brands, and carries a range of processing supplies including seasonings, vacuum bags, casings, and butcher knives. No facility size or headcount figures are provided.

Customers include commercial meat processors that need equipment to break down whole sides of beef into patties, as well as individual hunters looking for sausage stuffers and collagen casings for venison. The company addresses both industrial and retail demand.

