UPDATE companies SET description='Spectral Products is headquartered in Putnam, Connecticut, with additional offices in Albuquerque, New Mexico, and Seoul, South Korea. The company''s founding year and ownership structure are not publicly disclosed. It operates as a manufacturer of optical instrumentation.

The company designs and builds spectrometers, monochromators, light sources, integrating spheres, detectors, fiber-optic accessories, adapters, and filter wheels. Its product lines include the SM series of miniature spectrometers—such as the SM301/SM301-EX PbS(e) array spectrometer covering 1.0–3.0 µm and the TE-cooled SM304 InGaAs array spectrometer—the CM110 compact 1/8-meter monochromator with customizable slits, and the ASBN-W high-power tungsten-halogen light source assemblies featuring fused-silica lenses and UV-protected aluminum mirrors. An Optics Division also supplies optical coatings and coated optics for high-energy applications.

Spectral Products serves industrial, laboratory, research, and scientific markets, working directly with system designers and end users. The company maintains international representatives in Europe, Asia, and Australia.

The firm attributes its differentiation to an innovative direct-drive technique introduced more than a decade ago, which it says revolutionized computer-based spectrometers and monochromators by delivering high performance at lower cost. Its SM miniature spectrometers are marketed as combining essential features and optimal performance in a small footprint.', certifications=ARRAY['UL Listed']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Spectrometer manufacturing", "Monochromator manufacturing", "Light source assembly", "Optical coating", "Custom OEM design", "Integrating sphere fabrication", "Detector integration", "Fiber-optic accessory production", "Filter wheel manufacturing"], "industries": ["Industrial", "Laboratory", "Research", "Scientific", "System integration"], "materials": ["Fused silica", "UV-protected aluminum coating", "InGaAs", "PbS(e)", "Tungsten-halogen"], "equipment": ["SM301/SM301-EX PbS(e) array spectrometer", "SM304 TE-cooled InGaAs array spectrometer", "CM110 1/8-meter monochromator", "ASBN-W tungsten-halogen light source assembly"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Innovative direct-drive technique for spectrometers and monochromators", "High-performance instruments at lower cost", "Miniature spectrometer footprint with essential features", "Custom OEM spectrometer design capability", "Optical coatings and coated optics for high-energy components"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Putnam, CT; offices in Albuquerque, NM and Seoul, South Korea -> /", "Product offerings: spectrometers, monochromators, light sources, integrating spheres, detectors, fiber, adapters, filter wheels -> /", "Custom OEM spectrometers -> /", "SM product lines used worldwide -> /", "Direct drive technique introduced more than a decade ago -> /", "Specific products: SM301/SM301-EX, SM304, CM110, ASBN-W -> /", "International representatives in Europe, Asia, Australia -> /", "Optics Division: optical coatings and coated optics for high-energy component