UPDATE companies SET description='Staco Systems was founded in 1958 in Costa Mesa, California, originally operating as Staco Switch. The company began by supplying lighted pushbutton display switches to the aviation and defense firms clustered in Southern California, with its first Series 30 switch flying on a Fokker F-27 in 1960. Today the headquarters is in Irvine, California, and the firm maintains sales representatives in more than 35 countries.

The product line has expanded from those early switches to include rugged keyboards and keypads, electronic controllers, panel assemblies, edge‑lit panels, and complete cockpit control assemblies. Staco emphasizes custom engineering, citing advances in optics, weight reduction, and miniaturization as core technical capabilities. The company serves as a manufacturer of human‑machine interface components, producing both standard and custom solutions for demanding applications.

Staco’s customer base spans military, aerospace, shipboard, ground vehicle, naval, industrial, power‑generation, and flight‑simulation markets. The company references its long‑standing relationships with major aerospace and defense primes, though specific client names are not disclosed. Historical examples include the Fokker F‑27 installation and ongoing supply to military and commercial aviation programs.

Staco attributes its longevity to a commitment to quality and custom problem‑solving, backed by certifications such as AS9100 and MIL‑SPEC. The firm states that its differentiation lies in superior engineering and continual technology development that enable unique custom solutions tailored to customer specifications.', certifications=ARRAY['AS9100','AS9100C','ISO 9001','MIL-SPEC','MIL-PRF-22885','QS9000','TS-16949']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom HMI design and manufacturing", "Cockpit control assembly", "Illuminated panel and bezel fabrication", "Pushbutton switch manufacturing", "Data entry solution design", "Rugged keyboard and keypad production", "Electronic controller manufacturing", "Panel assembly", "Edge\u2011lit panel fabrication", "Lighted pushbutton switch production", "Avionic switch manufacturing"], "industries": ["Aerospace", "Defense", "Military", "Shipboard", "Ground Vehicles", "Naval", "Industrial", "Power Products", "Flight Simulation", "Precision Industries"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Unique advances in optics, weight reduction, and miniaturization", "Custom solutions engineered to solve specific customer problems", "AS9100 and MIL\u2011SPEC certified quality system", "Over 60 years of experience in aerospace and defense", "Global sales network with representatives in 35+ countries"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1958 in Costa Mesa, California -> /about", "Originally named Staco Switch -> /about", "First Series 30 switch used on Fokker F-27 in 1960 -> /about", "Headquarters in Irvine, California -> /about", "Sales representatives in over 35 countries -> /about", "Products: lighted pushbutton switches, rugged keyboards, electronic controllers, panel assemblies, edge-lit panels -> /about", "Certifications: AS9100, MIL-SPEC -> /about", "Industries: military, aerospace, shipboard, ground vehicles, naval, industrial, power products, flight simulation -> /about, /", "Qua